{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":292966,"duration_api_ms":289686,"ttft_ms":3205,"ttft_stream_ms":2526,"time_to_request_ms":21,"num_turns":49,"result":"# Change Plan\n\n## Task Classification\n**Feature (extension)** — adds new read-only observability capability to the existing beacon subsystem; no existing behavior is modified.\n\n## Affected Cells\n\n| Cell | Files to Modify | What Changes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `salt` (root) | `salt/minion.py` | `Minion.manage_beacons()` gains a `\"status\"` dispatch entry; `Minion.beacons_refresh()` threads `beacon_status` through `Beacon` recreation |\n| `salt/modules` | `salt/modules/beacons.py` | New public function `status()` |\n| Unmodeled (`salt/beacons/__init__.py`) | `salt/beacons/__init__.py` | `Beacon.__init__` gains `beacon_status` param; `Beacon.process()` records fire outcomes; new `Beacon.get_beacon_status()` method |\n| Tests | `tests/pytests/unit/test_beacons.py`, `tests/pytests/unit/modules/test_beacons.py` | New test cases for status recording and the event round-trip |\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n`Beacon.process()` is the only place where a beacon's fire outcome (timestamp + error) is known, but that outcome is discarded after each cycle — never persisted, never queryable. All other beacon-management queries (`list`, `list_available`, etc.) follow a uniform fire-event/wait-for-completion-event round trip through `Minion.manage_beacons()`. No such round trip exists for \"did this beacon actually run, and did it error.\" (Full detail: Investigation Report, Confirmed Root Cause.)\n\n## Trace Summary\n`Beacon.process()` (fire attempt, `salt/beacons/__init__.py:189-203`) → new `self.beacon_status[mod]` write → `Beacon.get_beacon_status()` (new) → `Minion.manage_beacons()` funcs dispatch (`salt/minion.py:4162-4187`) ← `salt/modules/beacons.py:status()` (new) fires `manage_beacons` event and blocks on `/salt/minion/minion_beacons_status_complete`. Separately: `Minion.beacons_refresh()` (`salt/minion.py:3998-4015`) must carry `beacon_status` across `Beacon` instance replacement, exactly like `interval_map`.\n\n## Change Strategy\n1. **`salt/beacons/__init__.py`**\n   - `import time` at module top.\n   - `Beacon.__init__(self, opts, functions, interval_map=None, beacon_status=None)`: add `self.beacon_status = beacon_status if beacon_status is not None else {}`.\n   - In `process()`, immediately after the try/except that sets `error` (right after the error-event-append block, before `if not error:`), add `self.beacon_status[mod] = {\"last_run\": time.time(), \"last_error\": error}`. This fires exactly once per beacon per cycle it actually runs — skipped entirely for beacons gated out by interval/disable/disable-during-state-run, which is correct since those beacons didn't fire.\n   - Add `get_beacon_status(self, name=None, include_pillar=True, include_opts=True)`:\n     - Resolve the configured beacon set via the existing `_get_beacons(include_pillar, include_opts)` helper.\n     - If `name` is given and not in that configured set: fire `{\"complete\": False, \"comment\": f\"Beacon {name} is not currently configured.\"}` on the new tag and return `True` (mirrors the \"cannot X, not configured\" pattern used by `enable_beacon`/`disable_beacon`).\n     - Otherwise build `status = {bname: {\"last_run\": info[\"last_run\"], \"last_error\": info[\"last_error\"]} if (info := self.beacon_status.get(bname)) else {\"last_run\": None, \"last_error\": None} for bname in (names to report)}` and fire `{\"complete\": True, \"beacon_status\": status}` on tag `/salt/minion/minion_beacons_status_complete`.\n     - Return `True` (matches every sibling method's return convention).\n\n2. **`salt/minion.py`**\n   - `Minion.manage_beacons()`: add to the `funcs` dict: `\"status\": (\"get_beacon_status\", {\"name\": name, \"include_opts\": include_opts, \"include_pillar\": include_pillar})`. No other change to this method — `name`, `include_opts`, `include_pillar` are already extracted from `data` at the top of the function.\n   - `Minion.beacons_refresh()`: add `prev_beacon_status = {}` then `if hasattr(self, \"beacons\") and hasattr(self.beacons, \"beacon_status\"): prev_beacon_status = self.beacons.beacon_status`, and pass `beacon_status=prev_beacon_status` into the `salt.beacons.Beacon(...)` constructor call alongside `interval_map=prev_interval_map`.\n\n3. **`salt/modules/beacons.py`**\n   - Add `status(name=None, include_pillar=True, include_opts=True, **kwargs)`, structured identically to `list_()`: open a listening event bus, fire `{\"func\": \"status\", \"name\": name, \"include_pillar\": include_pillar, \"include_opts\": include_opts}` on tag `\"manage_beacons\"`, wait on `/salt/minion/minion_beacons_status_complete`, return `event_ret[\"beacon_status\"]` when `event_ret[\"complete\"]` is true, otherwise return the existing `{\"result\": False, \"comment\": ...}` shape (using `event_ret[\"comment\"]` when present, else a timeout message) — matching `enable_beacon`'s not-complete branch. Wrap in the same `try/except KeyError` used by every sibling function for \"Event module not available.\"\n   - Docstring includes a CLI example: `salt '*' beacons.status` and `salt '*' beacons.status ps`, and documents that a beacon with `last_run: None` has never fired.\n\n4. **Tests**\n   - `tests/pytests/unit/test_beacons.py`: extend/add a test on `Beacon.process()` asserting `beacon.beacon_status[\"watch_apache\"][\"last_error\"]` is set after the existing exception-raising scenario, and a companion success-path test asserting `last_error is None` and `last_run` is a float. Add a test verifying a beacon absent from `opts[\"beacons\"]` (or not yet processed) is absent from `beacon_status` — i.e., \"never fired\" is representable as \"key absent,\" which `get_beacon_status` translates into `{\"last_run\": None, \"last_error\": None}`.\n   - `tests/pytests/unit/modules/test_beacons.py`: add `test_status()` following the exact `test_delete()`/`test_disable()` shape — mock `event.fire`, patch `SaltEvent.get_event` with a `side_effect` list containing one dict for tag `/salt/minion/minion_beacons_status_complete`, assert `beacons.status()` returns the `beacon_status` payload.\n\n## Specification Impact\n**None.** No CODEMANIFEST documents `Minion.manage_beacons`, `Minion.beacons_refresh`, or any function in `salt/modules/beacons.py` (confirmed in Investigation Report: root `salt` CODEMANIFEST documents only `_load_modules`/`sync_connect_master`/`tune_in`; `salt/modules` CODEMANIFEST documents only `__virtual__`/`run`/`ping`/`get_hash` as a 3-of-267 sample). `salt/beacons/__init__.py` has no CODEMANIFEST at all. No manifest file requires modification. Manifest Reconciliation (pipeline Step 7) will confirm this remains true post-implementation rather than silently drifting — i.e., verify the new code doesn't contradict any documented `Minion`/`salt/modules` algorithm text, which it does not since it only adds new, independent branches.\n\n## Usage Impact\n**None.** No `.goga/usages/` or cell-level `<cell>/.usages/` files exist for `salt`, `salt/modules`, or `salt/beacons` (confirmed in Investigation Report's Affected Usages table — table is empty by fact, not omission). Nothing to update.\n\n## Compatibility Verification\n**Backward compatible.** Verified per Investigation Report's Breaking Change Assessment (all 6 questions: NO). This plan does not alter any existing dict key, signature default, return shape, or dispatch entry — it only adds new ones. All existing `Beacon(...)` construction call sites (`salt/minion.py:4586`, `4604`, `4013`) remain valid unchanged since `beacon_status` is an optional keyword parameter defaulting to `None`→`{}`.\n\n## Test Strategy\n- **Unit, `Beacon.process()`**: verify `self.beacon_status[mod]` is populated with `last_run` (float) and `last_error` (`None` on success, exception string on failure) exactly when a beacon fires this cycle; verify it is *not* populated for beacons skipped by interval-gating or invalid config (so `get_beacon_status` correctly reports those as never-fired until they actually run).\n- **Unit, `Beacon.get_beacon_status()`**: never-configured explicit `name` → `complete: False` with a clear comment; configured-but-never-fired beacon → `{\"last_run\": None, \"last_error\": None}`; fired beacon → real values reflected verbatim from `self.beacon_status`.\n- **Unit, `salt/modules/beacons.py:status()`**: event-fire/wait round trip returns the `beacon_status` payload on success; \"Event module not available\" `KeyError` path returns `{\"result\": False, \"comment\": ...}` like every sibling function.\n- **Regression**: run existing `tests/pytests/unit/test_beacons.py` and `tests/pytests/unit/modules/test_beacons.py` unchanged to confirm no existing assertion breaks (per Compatibility Verification, none should).\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Forgetting to thread `beacon_status` through `beacons_refresh()`, silently losing history on every refresh | Medium (easy to miss, refresh is not the obvious call site) | High (defeats the \"not require restart/config touch\" requirement — refresh is far more frequent than restart) | Explicit constructor param + explicit `hasattr` guard mirroring the proven `interval_map` pattern; covered by a dedicated test asserting status survives a simulated `beacons_refresh()` call |\n| Recording status for beacons gated out by interval/state-run logic, making \"last_run\" lie about actual execution | Low | Medium (defeats \"reflect real beacon activity\") | Status write placed only in the branch reached after the fire attempt itself, not in any gating branch — verified by test asserting un-fired (gated) beacons are absent from `beacon_status` |\n| New tag name colliding with an existing tag or existing test's `side_effect` sequence | Low | Low (would surface immediately as test failure) | New tag `/salt/minion/minion_beacons_status_complete` chosen distinct from all 8 existing `/salt/minion/minion_beacon(s)_*_complete` tags; grep-verified no collision |\n| `status()` module function name colliding conceptually with the existing `salt/beacons/status.py` *beacon plugin* (a monitoring beacon type) | Low | Low (different namespace — `beacons.status` execution-module function vs. a beacon named \"status\" a user could configure) | Namespaces don't collide in code (module function vs. loader-dispatched beacon plugin); documented explicitly in the new docstring to avoid operator confusion |\n\nDo you approve the plan? Proceed to implementation?","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b0b7a9bd-9121-45a8-b91c-0a5bbda2c4d9","total_cost_usd":1.6138065,"usage":{"input_tokens":54,"cache_creation_input_tokens":107041,"cache_read_input_tokens":2031545,"output_tokens":24129,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":107041,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":54,"outputTokens":24129,"cacheReadInputTokens":2031545,"cacheCreationInputTokens":107041,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.6138065,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f319d4ba-7fc6-4931-be16-e6b6d3ed891d"}
